WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.870
Red-hot lava is still shooting into the air
from a volcano on the Spanish island of La

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.870
Palma.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:11.670
During a visit to the island, Spanish Prime
Minister Pedro Sanchez pledged government

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:17.960
aid to rebuild, even as there's no sign of
the eruption diminishing.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.790
La Palma's volcano won't let up.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:28.810
It's been spewing molten rock into the air
for weeks.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:34.750
In the smoldering light of day, you can barely
see through the smoke and the burning ash.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:40.000
The volcano has burst back into life after
50 years, and some of the residents are trying

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.070
their best to take it all in their stride.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.070
"A lot of people lost everything and this
is a demon for them.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.040
I see things a bit more rationally here.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.780
I can't change it but I have to keep going
with the things I still have, we have to keep

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.790
living."

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:09.600
The Cumbre Vieja volcano has already destroyed
almost a thousand buildings, and the lava

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.080
continues to threaten nearby communities.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.400
Spain's government has offered support, and
is set to approve more than 200 million euros

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.550
in aid this week.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:27.580
"We do not know when the volcanic eruption
will end, but what the people of La Palma

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:33.430
should know is that, regardless of when this
ends, the Spanish government, all the institutions,

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:38.409
will be there to face the enormous task of
rebuilding La Palma and to offer a horizon

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:47.690
of prosperity, progress and tranquility to
the people of La Palma."

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:52.770
The island's residents have already received
some emergency funds: immediate assistance

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.780
for those who have lost their homes.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.840
But, this is an island that relies heavily
on tourism.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.119
Something the local government has been keen
to emphasize.

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:11.319
"I would like to say at this point that the
best way to help La Palma is to treat us normally,

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:16.810
to visit us, to help us to stimulate the economy,
that our hotels are in business, that the

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:22.560
restaurants and cafes are open, that taxi
drivers, farmers and traders, all of us can

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.079
all reactivate the economy."

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:31.829
The explosive activity in the vents of the
volcano intensified on Sunday, causing several

00:02:31.829 --> 00:02:34.139
minor earthquakes nearby.

00:02:34.139 --> 00:02:40.170
So far, no casualties have been reported – thanks,
mainly, to speedy evacuation efforts.

